     4→ * CONTRACT: fileUri MUST be a file:// URI. The native layer emits
     5→ * onPlayerError immediately if a non-file:// URI is passed.
     6→ * Always use SafReaderModule.copyFileToCache() before calling this.
     7→ *
     8→ * Available only on Android custom dev-client / EAS builds (native module).
     9→ * Returns null on iOS, web, and any Android build where ExoPlayerPackage
    10→ * was not compiled in.
    11→ *
    12→ * ── HOW AVAILABILITY IS DETECTED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    13→ * requireNativeComponent in Fabric (new arch) does NOT validate the native
    14→ * side at module-load time.  It creates a component stub that is registered
    15→ * with NativeComponentRegistry; absence of the underlying view manager is
    16→ * only detected during React's completeWork phase — at render time — when
    17→ * Fabric calls ReactNativeViewConfigRegistry.get() and throws
    18→ * "View config not found for component ExoPlayerView".
    19→ *
    20→ * UIManager.hasViewManagerConfig() queries the NATIVE UIManager registry
    21→ * synchronously at module-load time.  If the Java ExoPlayerViewManager class
    22→ * is not compiled and registered, it returns false immediately — before any
    23→ * render attempt.  We use this as the primary gate:
    24→ *
    25→ *   hasViewManagerConfig → false  → NativeExoPlayerView stays null
    26→ *                                    isAvailable() → false
    27→ *                                    ExoPlayerView renders nothing
    28→ *                                    ViewerItem goes straight to expo-video
    29→ *                                    No ERROR ever appears in the log
    30→ *
    31→ *   hasViewManagerConfig → true   → requireNativeComponent runs
    32→ *                                    isAvailable() → true
    33→ *                                    ExoPlayerView renders the native TextureView
    34→ *
    35→ * ExoPlayerBoundary is kept as a belt-and-suspenders catch for any OEM where
    36→ * the registry check is unreliable, but it should never be needed in practice.
    37→ */
